                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54471aa8-de51-3749-889b-77a954443add",
                        "entry_id": "ea558d5b-10d3-3d52-a906-70bd339e0297",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Agir, penser en païen."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e03ac046-1f92-460c-9b2b-4338c294eb1f",
                                "sense_id": "54471aa8-de51-3749-889b-77a954443add",
                                "text": "Et, parce que je propose ce même principe que nul n’a nié…. je suis un païen [d’après Fénelon], je ne songe plus que je parle au milieu de l’Église, je paganise dans le sanctuaire."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "115cc454-72c4-3a02-9ea5-41ba48ed9505",
                        "entry_id": "ea558d5b-10d3-3d52-a906-70bd339e0297",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Donner le caractère du paganisme."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "91e589e5-0fd3-4b02-b5c4-4aa24ece9148",
                                "sense_id": "115cc454-72c4-3a02-9ea5-41ba48ed9505",
                                "text": "Sa statue [d’Adrien], celles de Jupiter capitolin et d’autres divinités grecques et phéniciennes ornèrent le temple bâti sur les ruines du sanctuaire de Jéhovah…. il fit aussi construire un temple de Jupiter sur Garizim, la montagne sainte des Samaritains, et un temple de Vénus sur le Golgotha ; on eût dit qu’il voulait ainsi paganiser les trois monts vénérés par les trois religions issues du monothéisme d’Israël."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "092f583c-ccaf-4f18-8265-ffe9a84c97ab",
                        "source_entry_id": "ea558d5b-10d3-3d52-a906-70bd339e0297",
                        "target_lang_word": "paganize",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "paganize",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1aeba343-b767-30c4-824b-fb7ebcea39e4",
                                        "entry_id": "75841fec-14ed-3280-80f3-8c336184188c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To convert (someone) to paganism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "55c4115d-8937-3cc3-8293-e45a629b3510",
                                        "entry_id": "75841fec-14ed-3280-80f3-8c336184188c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To behave like a pagan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8be81593-f3dd-4034-a45c-83689bc48655",
                                                "sense_id": "55c4115d-8937-3cc3-8293-e45a629b3510",
                                                "text": "This was that which made the old Christians paganize, while by their scandalous and base conforming to Heathenism they did no more, when they had done their utmost, but bring some Pagans to christianize; for true Christians they neither were themselves, nor could make other such in this fashion."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
